IPlayerContext.allowWaterBucketFall() (default: the allowWaterBucketFall setting, as upstream): the cost model asks the player context whether the bot may plan a fall broken by a water bucket, so a host can refuse it per player (a dimension where water evaporates, other than the Nether that Baritone already excludes) instead of through the one JVM-wide setting.

diff --git a/src/api/java/baritone/api/utils/IPlayerContext.java b/src/api/java/baritone/api/utils/IPlayerContext.java
index b537b07..826b0ad 100644
--- a/src/api/java/baritone/api/utils/IPlayerContext.java
+++ b/src/api/java/baritone/api/utils/IPlayerContext.java
@@ -132,6 +132,16 @@ public interface IPlayerContext {
         return true;
     }
 
+    /**
+     * Whether this player may plan a fall that is broken by placing water from a carried water bucket ({@link baritone.api.Settings#allowWaterBucketFall}
+     * is one value for the whole JVM). Defaults to that setting; a host whose players may not place water where they stand (a dimension
+     * in which water evaporates that is not the Nether, which Baritone already excludes) or that has switched the move off for one player
+     * overrides it per player.
+     */
+    default boolean allowWaterBucketFall() {
+        return BaritoneAPI.getSettings().allowWaterBucketFall.value;
+    }
+
     default Rotation playerRotations() {
         return new Rotation(player().getYRot(), player().getXRot());
